{
  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "It has not been demonstrated that the loft bedroom would provide adequate floor-to-ceiling heights and therefore provide an acceptable quality of accommodation for future occupiers. In the absence of this information, the proposal would be contrary to Policies DMD 5 (Residential Extensions) and DMD 8 (Houses in Multiple Occupation) of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Chapter 12 of the NPPF (2024).",
    "The proposed internal layout would give rise to an unacceptable fire safety risk. The ground-floor bedroom is accessed from the dining room and, although a secondary door leads to the rear garden, an occupant would be required to navigate at least two additional doors or gates in order to reach the front of the property in the event of a fire. This configuration fails to provide a safe, convenient and direct means of escape and does not demonstrate that the development would achieve an appropriate level of fire safety for future occupants. As such, the proposal fails to comply with Policy D12 (Fire Safety) of the London Plan (2021).\r",
    "The site is identified as being at risk of surface water flooding during a 1 in 100-year event plus 17% climate change allowance. In the absence of a Flood Risk Assessment (FRA), the application fails to demonstrate that the proposed development would be safe for its lifetime without increasing flood risk elsewhere. Specifically, no information has been provided to confirm that finished floor levels (FFL) would be set at least 150mm above the 1 in 100-year (plus climate change) surface water flood depth, below which ground-floor bedrooms would not be acceptable. No Flood Management/Evacuation Plan has been submitted to demonstrate that a safe route of escape, classified as Very Low Hazard under FD2320, would be available during a flood event. Furthermore, the proposal does not incorporate flood-resistant or flood-resilient measures, nor does it demonstrate the provision or retrofitting of SuDS or soft landscaping features to manage the existing flood risk at the site. In the absence of this information, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the development would be safe from flooding or that flood risk would not be increased elsewhere, contrary to guidance in Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021); Policies SI 12 and SI13 of the London Plan (2021); Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD59, DMD60 and DMD61 of the Development Management Document (2014).\r",
    "The proposed cycle parking would only be accessible via the dwelling, which is unacceptable. It has not been demonstrated that the required cycle parking could be provided on site without creating a cramped or cluttered appearance in the front garden or adversely affecting light to habitable rooms. As a result, the proposal fails to provide secure and accessible cycle storage and does not adequately facilitate or encourage sustainable travel. The development is therefore contrary to Policy DMD 45 (Parking Standards and Layout) of the Development Management Document (2014) and Policy T5 of the London Plan (2021), and Section 9 of the NPPF 2024."
  ],
